            "id": "380165160"
          },
          "hints": [
            {
              "content": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "At the equivalence point for this titration, the initial amount of HClO and OH"
                    },
                    {
                      "sup": true,
                      "text": "–"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " have been completely neutralized. However, the ClO"
                    },
                    {
                      "sup": true,
                      "text": "–"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " produced will react with H"
                    },
                    {
                      "sub": true,
                      "text": "2"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "O to form the weak acid and OH"
                    },
                    {
                      "sup": true,
                      "text": "–"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": ", according to the following reaction: "
                    },
                    {
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": " ",
                          "type": "text"
                        }
                      ],
                      "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                      "src": "\\mathrm{ClO}^-\\;+\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;\\mathrm{OH}^-\\;+\\;\\mathrm{HClO}",
                      "subtype": "latex",
                      "type": "formula_inline"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "id": "guwoj1vka442roe",
                  "type": "p"
                }
              ],
              "id": "1144196235"
            },
            {
              "content": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "First the moles and then concentration of ClO"
                    },
                    {
                      "sup": true,
                      "text": "–"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " produced, given the amounts of analyte and titrant, must be determined. An ICE table can be used to determine relative equilibrium concentrations of the species, and then the "
                    },
                    {
                      "em": true,
                      "text": "K"
                    },
                    {
                      "sub": true,
                      "text": "b"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " expression can be used to calculate [OH"
                    },
                    {
                      "sup": true,
                      "text": "–"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "]"
                    },
                    {
                      "sub": true,
                      "text": "eq"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": " and then pOH and pH."
                    }
                  ],
                  "id": "cuo8ppq07lemtfl",
                  "type": "p"
                }
              ],
              "id": "1347303167"
            },
